From f365efb1db2fca762ea95bcb45a583da768c26d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:10:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add Java (Temurin JDK) + Apache Maven for iDempiere ERP
 support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

baobab-erp's ERP engine migration to iDempiere requires a JDK and Maven
3.9.x in the baobab-dev `full` profile — no other BAOBAB engine needs
either today. Adds OpenJDK 17 via Eclipse Temurin's own apt repository
(confirmed multi-arch: amd64 + arm64), and Apache Maven 3.9.16 as an
explicitly pinned, SHA-512-verified tarball from archive.apache.org
(Maven Central's own "latest" currently resolves to a 4.0.0 pre-release,
which would be incompatible with iDempiere's documented 3.9.x
requirement).

Threads the new capability through the full pipeline this repo already
established: config/versions.yaml (source of truth) -> config/resolve.sh
(resolves + checksums into versions.lock) -> the Dockerfile's `final`
stage (installs + wires JAVA_HOME/PATH) -> config/capabilities.yaml
(contract self-declaration) -> scripts/verify.sh (build-time check).

Also fixes a copy/paste bug in the `base` stage's OCI LABEL block: the
image.source/image.documentation labels pointed at
github.com/nabhold/baobab-devcontainer, a repository name this project
has never used.

Targets baobab-dev:v1.3.0-rc.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014W3z8LMoe1iiMVZkCES5QT
